  "description": "ENOYIQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C81 H158 Ce9 Mn1 N8 O51,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce9 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.429-4.143 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.09-141.06°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C81H158Ce9MnN8O51·2MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV), Mn(III).",
